From 26d90ffa7a18f11957b37815185f6943d13a473b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 03:34:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix security issues found in audit: stored XSS, SSRF, filter
 injection, vuln deps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- static/index.html: escape recipe/shopping-list data (title, ingredients,
  instructions, item names, URLs) before interpolating into document.write()
  in the print handlers. This content can originate from scraped or
  manually-imported third-party recipe pages, so it was a stored XSS vector.
  Also drop non-http(s) hrefs (safeHref) to block javascript:/data: links.

- app/url_safety.py (new) + routers/recipes.py: validate source_url before
  the /api/recipes/import endpoint hands it to Mealie's URL importer.
  Mealie fetches the URL server-side on our behalf and sits on the same
  trusted LAN, so an unvalidated URL was an SSRF vector against internal
  services. Rejects non-http(s) schemes and hosts resolving to
  private/loopback/link-local/reserved IPs.

- mealie_client.py: escape quotes in values interpolated into Mealie
  queryFilter strings (orgURL / tags.name lookups) so a URL or tag name
  containing a `"` can't break out of the filter and inject clauses.

- requirements.txt: bump fastapi, starlette, requests, python-multipart,
  lxml, and lxml-html-clean to versions with no known CVEs (verified via
  pip-audit — 22 known vulnerabilities down to 0). Verified the app still
  imports and boots cleanly against the updated dependency set.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
